1
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:07,804
Carbon credits only work if one credit means one tonne.

2
00:00:07,844 --> 00:00:11,498
Today the same credit can be sold twice, retired twice,

3
00:00:11,538 --> 00:00:17,005
claimed by a host country and a company at once, or never
have been issued at all.

4
00:00:17,045 --> 00:00:21,706
Banks solved this a century ago with a daily three-way
reconciliation.

5
00:00:21,746 --> 00:00:23,385
Carbon markets never did.

6
00:00:23,425 --> 00:00:24,393
This is VERDIQ:

7
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:26,206
every tonne, verified once.

8
00:00:27,046 --> 00:00:31,366
Everything you will see is synthetic data, generated for
this demo,

9
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:34,489
with eight kinds of fraud deliberately injected.

10
00:00:34,529 --> 00:00:38,654
VERDIQ reconciles all six hundred and fifty-three ledger
events,

11
00:00:38,694 --> 00:00:43,013
and all 8 injected fraud types were detected in our
synthetic test,

12
00:00:43,053 --> 00:00:45,681
with no false alarms on the clean trades.

13
00:00:45,721 --> 00:00:51,473
In this market, about fifty-five thousand tonnes of claims
would have been counted twice:

14
00:00:51,513 --> 00:00:58,045
roughly one and a half million dollars of volume, the
yearly emissions of about twelve thousand cars.

15
00:00:58,085 --> 00:01:01,819
Like a bank balance, every issuance balances to the tonne:

16
00:01:01,859 --> 00:01:05,138
issued equals unsold, plus in market, plus retired.

17
00:01:05,178 --> 00:01:08,326
The coral hexagons are tonnes the ledger refused.

18
00:01:09,166 --> 00:01:15,565
The same eight thousand tonnes circle between three
trading desks in three weeks while the price doubles.

19
00:01:15,605 --> 00:01:17,283
That is a wash-trading loop.

20
00:01:17,323 --> 00:01:21,882
Select a node, and you get every flag with its rule,
severity and evidence.

21
00:01:21,922 --> 00:01:27,524
Coral lines mark flows that broke a rule, and the node
size shows how many tonnes it traded.

22
00:01:27,564 --> 00:01:30,652
The Time Machine replays the market month by month.

23
00:01:30,692 --> 00:01:35,926
Fraud events pop in at the moment they occur, and the
protected-tonnes curve steps up.

24
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:43,218
Two Sundarbans projects claim thirty-one percent of the
same mangrove polygon,

25
00:01:43,258 --> 00:01:48,044
and a Cusco project claims one hundred seventy-three
tonnes per hectare where

26
00:01:48,084 --> 00:01:49,924
the physical ceiling is forty.

27
00:01:49,964 --> 00:01:55,063
Every project gets a zero to one hundred trust score, with
a plain-English reason.

28
00:01:55,103 --> 00:01:58,949
The vegetation series here is simulated, and labelled as
such.

29
00:01:58,989 --> 00:02:00,014
Now greenwashing.

30
00:02:00,054 --> 00:02:05,843
Meridian Airways, a fictional company, told the press it
offset four hundred thousand tonnes.

31
00:02:05,883 --> 00:02:10,292
The ledger shows about one hundred twenty-six thousand
validly retired,

32
00:02:10,332 --> 00:02:15,431
and only about one hundred thirteen thousand from credits
with no integrity flags.

33
00:02:15,471 --> 00:02:18,690
Roughly twenty-eight percent of the claim is backed.

34
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,833
Now the part that matters.

35
00:02:23,873 --> 00:02:26,921
A fraudster tries to double-count credits, live.

36
00:02:26,961 --> 00:02:32,069
That was a real transaction against our Solidity registry
on a local test chain.

37
00:02:32,109 --> 00:02:38,504
The contract reverted it with a reason code, and here is
the transaction hash, in about two seconds.

38
00:02:38,544 --> 00:02:43,909
Independently, the reconciliation engine flagged it, with
the rule and the evidence.

39
00:02:43,949 --> 00:02:47,705
Without VERDIQ, these tonnes would have been counted
twice.

40
00:02:47,745 --> 00:02:48,091
Again:

41
00:02:48,131 --> 00:02:48,992
a double sale.

42
00:02:49,032 --> 00:02:50,536
And a double retirement.

43
00:02:50,576 --> 00:02:54,719
Every attempt is blocked, counted, and added to the impact
total.

44
00:02:54,759 --> 00:02:58,451
The log shows who tried it, how many tonnes were at stake,

45
00:02:58,491 --> 00:03:02,376
the reason code, and the transaction that carried the
revert.

46
00:03:11,367 --> 00:03:12,653
Banks close the day.

47
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:14,377
Now carbon markets do too:

48
00:03:14,417 --> 00:03:18,356
every month-end snapshot is a Merkle root anchored
on-chain.

49
00:03:18,396 --> 00:03:23,794
Pick any serial and prove it with a handful of hashes,
without seeing the dataset.

50
00:03:23,834 --> 00:03:28,105
Watch what happens when one field of the record is
tampered with:

51
00:03:28,145 --> 00:03:31,354
the proof fails, and the original verifies again.

52
00:03:31,394 --> 00:03:36,129
Every credit range also gets a passport, with its
timeline, owner chain,

53
00:03:36,169 --> 00:03:40,904
trust score, Merkle proof, and the transaction hash of any
blocked sale.

54
00:03:40,944 --> 00:03:44,750
The QR code opens a public page with no login, so a buyer,

55
00:03:44,790 --> 00:03:48,663
a journalist or a regulator can verify a credit in
seconds.

56
00:03:57,557 --> 00:04:01,874
VERDIQ turns carbon credits from promises into audited
facts:

57
00:04:01,914 --> 00:04:08,231
reconciled daily, blocked on a chain, and verifiable by
anyone, in Bangla and in English.

58
00:04:08,271 --> 00:04:13,302
All data in this demo is synthetic, the vegetation signal
is simulated,

59
00:04:13,342 --> 00:04:17,373
and we claim no partnership with any registry or company.

60
00:04:17,413 --> 00:04:19,301
Every tonne, verified once.
